# Token diet (global)

Reduce per-turn context without changing product behavior.

## Shell output

- When `rtk` is on PATH, prefer `rtk <cmd>` for noisy commands. If missing: `bob-ensure rtk` once, or redirect to `/tmp/` and `tail -25`.
- Never paste build, docker, or gradle logs longer than 30 lines into chat.

## File reads

- Follow `graft-code-map.mdc`: Graft crux or skeleton first; max **80 lines** per `Read`; open only at Graft-identified spans.

## context-mode MCP

- When the `context-mode` server is available, use it to virtualize large tool outputs instead of inlining full blobs.

## Turn budget (soft)

- Avoid more than 15 tool calls before reporting blockers; prefer `graft_trace_calls` over repeated greps.
